   "external": "",
   "query": "Gemini"
  },
  {
   "text": "I think, very ironically, the main problem with LLM software is *attention*; your most valuable commodity in any project is people paying attention to the thing and feeding the results of that attention back into the project, and LLMs make it easy for humans to stop paying attentions so results suck",
   "handle": "unormal.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "🐔 Brian Bucklew 🐔 ₑͤ＞∿＜ₑͤ ∞🌮",
   "likes": 289,
   "reposts": 37,
